  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x1004">
    <title>Limiter hardness (hard cut threshold) [CAUTION] (c_add_n_max_fcut)</title>
    <description>c_add_n_max_fcut | change with care | risk medium&#013;&#010;Stock: 50 to 50 rpm&#013;&#010;Allowed by ms45_check.py: 0 to 100&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;How far the engine may go above the rev limit before the controller sets the torque request to 0.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Recipe: Stock 50. 30 = slightly harder, 15 = clearly harder, 10 = hard. Not below 10. Fault 28B1/28B2: back to 50.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Code 0x545A0: rpm &gt; limit + value sets the request to 0 until rpm &lt;= limit. This is the bounce width: smaller = faster, harder bouncing (d-d-d instead of a soft hum). Cylinder cut at 0 Nm is traced close to the injector output. Runs in the 10 ms task.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Together with: Works together with P/I gain and prediction time. Harder bouncing loads drivetrain and bearings more.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Test: Warm, standing, in steps 30, 15, 10. Below 15 there is little extra effect. Read fault memory after each step.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x457D4" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>rpm</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1005" flags="0x0">
    <title>Limiter prediction time, manual [CAUTION] (id_t_n_max_pred_mt__gear)</title>
    <description>id_t_n_max_pred_mt__gear | change with care | risk low&#013;&#010;Stock: 0.03125 to 0.1875 s&#013;&#010;Allowed by ms45_check.py: 0 to 0.3&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;The controller predicts rpm this far ahead and intervenes earlier.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Recipe: Hard cut step 3: set all cells to 0 together with threshold 10.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Code 0x544DC: used for the predicted rpm. 0 = intervene only at the real limit. Little effect on bounce frequency in the model.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Together with: Smaller makes the limiter entry more abrupt.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Test: Log rpm at the limiter.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x45251" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="8" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
